{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GYSfymp61QvJ3nFTm7oH3Y","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/runbooks/gate-2.md:82:   draft (the merger marks PRs ready from Phase 2), so mark it ready, then\ndocs/proposal.md:312:**The merger takes it from here.** Once tests pass, the controller marks the PR ready for review; the merger lands it when every requested review passes.\ndocs/proposal.md:322:5. **Close-out.** The controller posts one PR review at the pinned commit (event `COMMENT`): findings on lines the PR added are inline comments, every other finding is listed in the review body. If GitHub answers 422 (a line or the commit is not in the PR), it posts the review again with every finding in the body, and if that is also refused, as a plain PR comment. It commits `review-<role>.md` and the run's redacted output to the PR branch through the per-branch committer (no `[skip ci]`: PR-branch commits always run CI so required checks report on the head), and swaps `:running` for `:done` or `:changes`. The reviewer never marks the PR ready and never edits it; the merger does.\ninternal/reviewer/doc.go:45:// stays and the review runs again. The loop never marks the PR ready and never\n     engineer's section\n   - a \"ready for approval\" comment. **Read `.ard/<n>/plan.md`**, then add\n     `ard:approved` yourself (it counts only from a human with triage\n     permission, added after triage finished)\n   - `ard:worker:engineer:running`, a `worker/<n>-…` branch and a draft PR\n   - `ard:review:eng-review` on the PR, then a PR review and\n     `ard:review:eng-review:done` or `:changes`\n6. **Merge** the PR by hand once you are satisfied: the worker opens it as a\n   draft (the merger marks PRs ready from Phase 2), so mark it ready, then\n   **Squash and merge**. Stop `serve` with Ctrl-C (SIGINT); it stops cleanly\n   between jobs.\n\n**Moving faster than the poll.** Each loop ticks once at startup, then every\ninterval (triage 15 min, workers and reviewers 5 min). To act now, send\n`SIGUSR1` to `serve` (`kill -USR1 <pid of ard serve>`): every loop runs one tick\nimmediately, still behind the kill switch and the job pool, and logs\n`controller.wake`. No restart is needed.\n// files and logs) and the sidecar are untrusted too.\n//\n// # The verdict\n//\n// The agent writes only .ard/<issue#>/review-<role>.md; close-out rejects any\n// other change (WritableFor). Code edits are never collected. Close-out posts\n// one COMMENT review at the pinned commit (inline comments on lines the PR\n// added, everything else in the body) and swaps the label: :done, :changes, or\n// (an approve on a head that gained code meanwhile) neither, so the request\n// stays and the review runs again. The loop never marks the PR ready and never\n// edits it; #46 does.\n//\n// In --dry-run the loop logs review.would_claim and stops: no fetch, no job\n// row, no pool slot, no label.\npackage reviewer","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d56edd2a-39b2-4835-bbc3-49ea12ca5258","uuid":"9b540b63-77ba-4f9e-b8ff-88b844f29dc6","timestamp":"2026-11-23T14:34:41.424Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"docs/runbooks/gate-2.md:82:   draft (the merger marks PRs ready from Phase 2), so mark it ready, then\ndocs/proposal.md:312:**The merger takes it from here.** Once tests pass, the controller marks the PR ready for review; the merger lands it when every requested review passes.\ndocs/proposal.md:322:5. **Close-out.** The controller posts one PR review at the pinned commit (event `COMMENT`): findings on lines the PR added are inline comments, every other finding is listed in the review body. If GitHub answers 422 (a line or the commit is not in the PR), it posts the review again with every finding in the body, and if that is also refused, as a plain PR comment. It commits `review-<role>.md` and the run's redacted output to the PR branch through the per-branch committer (no `[skip ci]`: PR-branch commits always run CI so require