{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChL2TJXRhx7hY52T719zn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NmZRgjWvbGk2inYYkApNAR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\ndef sub(p,a,b):\n    s=open(p).read(); assert a in s,(p,a); open(p,'w').write(s.replace(a,b,1))\nsub('docs/proposal.md',\"**The merger takes it from here.** Once tests pass, the controller marks the PR ready for review; the merger lands it when every requested review passes.\",\n\"**The merger takes it from here.** A worker PR stays a draft until every requested review passes at its current head; then the controller marks it ready for review. The merger (Phase 2) merges ready PRs that also pass its gates.\")\nsub('docs/proposal.md',\"The reviewer never marks the PR ready and never edits it; the merger does.\",\n\"The reviewer never edits the PR. After a close-out (and on every tick, so a restart cannot miss it) the controller marks a draft worker PR ready for review once every requested review is `:done` at the PR's current head and no `:changes`, `:running`, `ard:executor:failed`, `ard:needs-human`, `ard:hold` or `ard:tests:failed` label is present; it never converts a PR back to draft and never merges, which stays with the merger (Phase 2) and humans.\")\nsub('docs/runbooks/gate-2.md',\"\"\"the worker opens it as a\n   draft (the merger marks PRs ready from Phase 2), so mark it ready, then\n   **Squash and merge**.\"\"\",\"\"\"the worker opens it as a\n   draft and the controller marks it ready once every requested review is\n   `:done` at the head, so just **Squash and merge**. (Mark it ready by hand\n   only to override a review that is still `:changes`.)\"\"\")\nsub('internal/reviewer/doc.go',\"\"\"The loop never marks the PR ready and never\n// edits it; #46 does.\"\"\",\"\"\"The loop never edits the PR.\n//\n// # Marking ready\n//\n// After each close-out, and on every tick (so a restart cannot miss it), the\n// loop marks a draft App PR on a worker/ branch ready for review when every\n// requested review role is :done at the PR's current head (the head recorded\n// by its newest claim, ignoring commits that only touch .ard/<issue>/), and\n// none of :changes, :running, ard:executor:failed, ard:needs-human, ard:hold or\n// ard:tests:failed is set. It logs review.marked_ready; a failed MarkReady is\n// logged and retried next tick, never failing close-out. In --dry-run only the\n// effects ledger gets a line. It never converts a PR back to draft and never\n// merges.\"\"\")\nE\ngrep -n \"marking it ready\" -B2 -A2 internal/worker/run.go; sed -n 40,60p internal/reviewer/doc.go"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1414,"cache_read_input_tokens":48062,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1414},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d56edd2a-39b2-4835-bbc3-49ea12ca5258","uuid":"c0a8af0e-8720-45d1-bcba-90ae422816f0","timestamp":"2026-11-23T14:34:47.179Z","request_id":"req_011ChL2TJPFHQeTefUwAtvQB"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NmZRgjWvbGk2inYYkApNAR","type":"tool_result","content":"712-\n713-// openPR creates or updates the draft PR and records it. The PR stays a draft:\n714:// marking it ready is the merger's. It reports false after finishing the job.\n715-func (jb *job) openPR(ctx context.Context, res *closeout.WorkerResult) bool {\n716-\td := jb.l.d\n// The agent writes only .ard/<issue#>/review-<role>.md; close-out rejects any\n// other change (WritableFor). Code edits are never collected. Close-out posts\n// one COMMENT review at the pinned commit (inline comments on lines the PR\n// added, everything else in the body) and swaps the label: :done, :changes, or\n// (an approve on a head that gained code meanwhile) neither, so the request\n// stays and the review runs again. The loop never edits the PR.\n//\n// # Marking ready\n//\n// After each close-out, and on every tick (so a restart cannot miss it), the\n// loop marks a draft App PR on a worker/ branch ready for review when every\n// requested review role is :done at the PR's current head (the head recorded\n// by its newest claim, ignoring commits that only touch .ard/<issue>/), and\n// none of :changes, :running, ard:executor:failed, ard:needs-human, ard:hold or\n// ard:tests:failed is set. It logs review.marked_ready; a failed MarkReady is\n// logged and retried next tick, never failing close-out. In --dry-run only the\n// effects ledger gets a line. It never converts a PR back to draft and never\n// merges.\n//\n// In --dry-run the loop logs review.would_claim and stops: no fetch, no job\n// row, no pool slot, no label.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d56edd2a-39b2-4835-bbc3-49ea12ca5258","uuid":"2fd3db7c-84eb-46d2-b59d-da28ccc87408","timestamp":"2026-11-23T14:34:47.238Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"712-\n713-// openPR creates or updates the draft PR and records it. The PR stays a draft:\n714:// marking it ready is the merger's. It reports false after finishing the job.\n715-func (jb *job) openPR(ctx context.Context, res *closeout.WorkerResult) bool {\n716-\td := jb.l.d\n// The agent writes only .ard/<issue#>/review-<role>.md; close-out rejects any\n// other change (WritableFor). Code edits are never collected. Close-out posts\n// one COMMENT review at the pinned commit (inline comments on lines the PR\n// added, everything else in the body) and swaps the label: :done, :changes, or\n// (an approve on a head that gained code meanwhile) neither, so the request\n// stays and the review runs again. The loop never edits the PR.\n//\n// # Marking ready\n//\n// After each close-out, and on every tick (so a restart cannot miss it), the\n// loop marks a draft App PR on a worker/ branch ready for review when every\n// requested review role is :done at the PR's current head (the head recorded\n// by its newest claim, ignoring commits that only touch .ard/<issue>/), and\n// none of :changes, :running, ard:executor:failed, ard:needs-human, ard:hold or\n// ard:tests:failed is set. It logs review.marked_ready; a failed MarkReady is\n// logged and retried next tick, never failing close-out. In --dry-run only the\n// effects ledger gets a line. It never converts a PR back to draft and never\n// merges.\n//\n// In --dry-run the loop logs review.would_claim and stops: no fetch, no job\n// row, no pool slot, no label.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NmZRgjWvbGk2inYYkApNAR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
