{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChL2XuAP1C87g9jTzW3pi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The reviewer loop now marks a worker's draft PR ready for review once every requested review is `:done` at its current head, and the docs are updated to match. `make test` and `make lint` pass. The planned end-to-end case in `internal/servecmd/reviewer_e2e_test.go` was not added, and no test calls `maybeReady` from `run` directly.\n\n- **Marking logic:** the new `internal/reviewer/ready.go` holds `maybeReady`, which applies the issue's rule. It calls `MarkReady` through the effects layer. A failure is logged as `review.mark_ready_failed` and retried on the next tick. It cannot fail close-out.\n- **When it runs:** after each reviewer close-out, and on every tick. The sweep runs before the model-credential check, so it also works with no credential and in dry-run, where only the ledger gets a line.\n- **Head check:** the reviewed head comes from each role's newest claim event. If there is no claim event, or git can't be read, the PR is not marked.\n- **Sweep search:** the fake GitHub client doesn't support `author:` or `draft:` search terms. The sweep therefore searches open PRs carrying a `:done` label for each reviewer role and filters the rest in code.\n- **Tests:** `internal/reviewer/ready_test.go` covers every case in the issue's checklist. The post-close-out call in `run` goes through the same `maybeReady` code as the sweep.\n- **Docs:** I updated the worker and reviewer sections of `docs/proposal.md`, the Gate 2 runbook merge step, `internal/reviewer/doc.go`, and a comment in `internal/worker/run.go`.\n\nThe report is in `.ard/194/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1166,"cache_read_input_tokens":52634,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":116